==English==
[[File:Silver Gull mouth.jpg|thumb|right|A Silver Gull squawking]]

===Etymology===
{{unk|en}} {{defdate|from 1821}}, but probably of imitative origin (compare dialectal {{cog|it|squacco||small-crested [[heron]]}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/skwɔːk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-squawk.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːk}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[shrill]] [[noise]], especially made by a [[voice]] or [[bird]]; a [[yell]], [[scream]], or [[call]].
# {{lb|en|aviation}} A four-digit transponder code used by aircraft for identification or transmission of emergency signals.
# {{lb|en|aviation}} An issue or complaint related to aircraft maintenance.
#* '''1969''', ''American Aviation'' (volume 32)
#*: We think instructors should stress the importance of writeups on all maintenance '''squawks''' after the completion of each flight. More important, something should be done by the aircraft operator to correct such '''squawks'''.
# The [[American night heron]].
# {{lb|en|programming|informal}} A [[warning]] [[message]] indicating a possible [[error]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Scott Meyers|title=Effective C++ Digital Collection: 140 Ways to Improve Your Programming|passage=The function-hiding code above, for instance, goes through a different (but widely used) compiler with nary a '''squawk'''.}}

