===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To make a squawking noise; to [[yell]], [[scream]], or call out [[shrilly]].
#* {{RQ:Orwell Animal Farm|6}}
#*: The hens woke up '''squawking''' with terror because they had all dreamed simultaneously of hearing a gun go off in the distance.
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive}} To [[speak out]]; to [[protest]].
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive}} To [[report]] an [[infraction]]; to [[rat]] on or [[tattle]]; to [[disclose]] a [[secret]].
#* '''1948''', Andrew Geer, ''The Sea Chase'' (page 68)
#*: "I'll slit your throat if you '''squawk''' on us," Krantz threatened.
# {{lb|en|programming|intransitive|informal}} To produce a [[warning]] [[message]], indicating a possible [[error]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Steve Maguire|title=Writing Solid Code|passage=That way, if you type = instead of ==, the compiler will '''squawk''' because you can't assign something to a constant.}}
#* '''2013''', Bill Sempf, ‎Chuck Sphar, ‎Stephen R. Davis, ''C# 5.0 All-in-One For Dummies''
#*: You want the compiler to '''squawk''' if you try to instantiate for a type that doesn't implement IPrioritizable.
# {{lb|en|aviation}} To set or transmit a four-digit [[transponder]] code. {{non-gloss definition|(Normally followed by the specific code in question.)}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang|dated}} To [[back out]] in a mean way. <!-- = funk it? -->

